{
  "id": "l1",
  "number": 1,
  "title": "Mikä tää on?",
  "subtitle": "What is this?",
  "tags": [
    "basics",
    "questions",
    "verbs"
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "intro",
      "text": "You already know your first sentence. You just heard it."
    },
    {
      "type": "phrase",
      "annotated": "{Mikä|grammar|Q-word|what} {tää|word|pronoun|this} {on|grammar|verb|is}?",
      "translation": "What is this?"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The magic word: on"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "{On|grammar|verb|is} means \"is.\" That's it. Finnish stacks words simply — no tricks to learn yet."
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "fi": "Tää {on|grammar|verb|is} kahvi.",
          "en": "This is coffee."
        },
        {
          "fi": "Tää {on|grammar|verb|is} auto.",
          "en": "This is a car."
        },
        {
          "fi": "Tää {on|grammar|verb|is} ongelma.",
          "en": "This is a problem."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "color": "tip",
      "title": "Anchoring Rule",
      "text": "Finnish has no \"a\" or \"the.\" Never mourn what a language lacks. Move on."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Now flip it — ask!"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "A",
          "fi": "Mikä tää on?",
          "en": "What is this?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "B",
          "fi": "Tää on kahvi.",
          "en": "This is coffee."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Add one word: hyvä"
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "fi": "Tää on {hyvä|word|adjective|good}.",
          "en": "This is good."
        },
        {
          "fi": "Tää kahvi on {hyvä|word|adjective|good}.",
          "en": "This coffee is good."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "pronunciation",
      "content": "ää sounds like the \"a\" in \"cat\" — but longer and more open. So tää rhymes with \"yeah\" said lazily. Try it: tääää."
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab",
      "rows": [
        {
          "fi": "on",
          "en": "is",
          "type": "grammar"
        },
        {
          "fi": "tää",
          "en": "this (colloquial)",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "fi": "mikä",
          "en": "what",
          "type": "word"
        },
        {
          "fi": "hyvä",
          "en": "good",
          "type": "word"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "checklist",
      "title": "What you now own",
      "items": [
        "on — is",
        "tää — this (real colloquial)",
        "mikä — what",
        "hyvä — good",
        "Word order: subject + on + complement"
      ]
    }
  ]
}